        "Study_Objective": "Assess carbonation curing of steel slag tailings after magnetic separation (dry powder SSD and wet mud SSW) and their seawater durability for artificial reefs.",
        "Abstract_or_Key_Finding": "After 24 h carbonation (20% CO2), CO2 uptake (CaO conversion) reached 33.5% (SSD) and 35.5% (SSW), strength 21 and 50 MPa. Carbonation plus hydration in SSD, only carbonation in SSW. Both lowest at 7 d seawater curing; SSD lost 30% after 56 d, SSW unchanged. CaO in carbonation-active minerals controls performance.",
